  "Formally established the medical condition name Aphantasia and standardized VVIQ diagnostic classification.": [
    "AboutView"
  ],
  "Established standard population norms: scores < 32 indicate marked aphantasia (score 16 = total aphantasia); population mean = 56.8.": [
    "AboutView"
  ],
  "Established hyperphantasia threshold (75-80 pts) and frontoparietal-occipitotemporal neuroplastic connectivity model.": [
    "AboutView"
  ],
  "Demonstrated that aphantasia can be unimodal (visual only) or multisensory (multi-modal attenuation).": [
    "AboutView"
  ],
  "Psychophysical binocular rivalry priming proving aphantasia is a genuine sensory absence rather than metacognitive bias.": [
    "AboutView"
  ],
  "Foundational basis for 6-week curriculum: demonstrated that structured Functional Imagery Training significantly increases imagery capacity.": [
